                can manually override the autoselected mode by adding media
                options to the appropriate hostname.if(5) file.

     1100bbaasseeTT    Set 10Mbps operation.  The ifconfig(8) mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can
                also be used to select either ffuullll--dduupplleexx or hhaallff--dduupplleexx
                modes.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX  Set 100Mbps (Fast Ethernet) operation.  The ifconfig(8)
                mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can also be used to select either ffuullll--dduupplleexx
                or hhaallff--dduupplleexx modes.

     The ttxxpp driver supports the following media options:

     ffuullll--dduupplleexx  Force full duplex operation.

     hhaallff--dduupplleexx  Force half duplex operation.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

